Carafe Lab: retain nvmap SMMU mappings while GPU mappings still pin their handles.
Guest handle release preserves the pin count and handle lookup until the last GPU unpin.
The CPU unlock result from patch 0018 stays independent of the GPU pin lifetime. Sparse
Remap intervals share pin owners across splits and release replaced or freed intervals
only after their GMMU mappings change. Address-space destruction releases its remaining
mappings. GPU devices retain the address-space owner until they close. Session teardown
retires user references and marks handles closed before destroying the heap mapper; late
unpins cannot access that mapper or a replacement session. Existing SMMU
Unmap invalidates renderer caches before unmapping and Free reuse.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

